1900 BM$="Vince: You have to hand in that report tomorrow, right? We're finally back\in London and you're already pulling an all-nighter.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1910 BM$="Clark: Eeyup. Got a call as soon as I stepped inside. `I need everything you\found out in Europe!` And it has to be ready by tomorrow at noon.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1920 BM$="Vince: But after that, the job's done, right? I sure hope the pay's good.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1930 BM$="Clark: Still... Who the heck is Susanna, really? After all that work, we only\have this slipshod report...":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1940 BM$="Vince: Come to think of it, Eleno Vision's last concert was something else.\First time I go to a concert where the singer starts yelling `Kill!` like that.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1950 BM$="Clark: Speaking of `kill`... I called a friend in Germany once we came back\here. That magician, Krost? He died that night. He started bleeding from\his forehead again.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1960 BM$="Vince: Huh. Well, his death couldn't be related to Susanna, could it? Are you\going to put that in the report too?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1970 BM$="Clark: The client wants me to report anything that catches my attention,\even if it doesn't strictly involve Susanna.":GOSUB 5100
1980 BM$="The two detectives continued to work over a cup of tea.":GOSUB 5100
